{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.BurnsideDischarge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BurnsideDischarge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionHookProductBridge","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionReindex","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.RSKBurnsideDischarge"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BurnsideDischarge.instBurnsideContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BurnsideDischarge.instBurnsideContext","kind":"instance","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BurnsideDischarge.lean#L103-L110","doc":"The `BurnsideContext` instance, now backed by `burnside_proved` instead of assumed.\n\nWith this in scope, `DeltaLambdaSignRule.burnside` is no longer conditional in practice:\nits class argument resolves to a derivation. The class itself is left in place upstream\n(removing it is an upstream edit and would churn every `[BurnsideContext]` signature);\nwhat changes is that it is now *inhabited by a proof*. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BurnsideDischarge.burnside_proved","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BurnsideDischarge.burnside_proved","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BurnsideDischarge.lean#L79-L101","doc":"**Burnside / RSK over the custom `Partition` encoding**, derived rather than assumed:\n`Σ_λ (f^λ)² = n!` for a `parts`-complete, `parts`-`Nodup` list of partitions of `n`.\n\nComposes bridge (1) (`dimIrrep_eq_numSYT`, axiom-clean), the shape glue above, bridge (2)\n(`sum_map_eq_sum_partitionIndex`, axiom-clean), and the Wedderburn dimension sum\n(`OVTopAssembly.sum_numSYT_sq_eq_factorial`).\n\n**Corrected 2026-08-23.** That last citation read *\"which carries the residual `sorryAx` — see the\nmodule docstring\"*. It does not: it carries a class hypothesis, `SnIsotypicSpechtSplit`, which is\nnow inhabited by `SnIsotypicSpechtSplitInstance`, and `#print axioms` on it reports\n`[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BurnsideDischarge.toYoungDiagram_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BurnsideDischarge.toYoungDiagram_eq","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BurnsideDischarge.lean#L66-L77","doc":"**The shape glue.** The `YoungDiagram` a custom `Partition n` denotes is the diagram\ncarried by its image under the reindexing equiv — i.e. bridge (1)'s `toYoungDiagram` and\nbridge (2)'s `partitionEquivIndex` agree on shapes.\n\nBoth sides are `YoungDiagram.ofRowLens` of the same parts list; the right-hand side takes\nthe scenic route through `Nat.Partition`'s multiset, which `sort_coe_parts` undoes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BurnsideDischarge.sort_coe_parts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BurnsideDischarge.sort_coe_parts","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BurnsideDischarge.lean#L58-L64","doc":"Coercing a weakly-decreasing list to a `Multiset` and sorting it back is the identity.\nThis is the same round-trip `PartitionNatBridge.partitionEquivNatPartition`'s `left_inv`\nperforms; isolated here because the shape identity below needs it on its own. ","signatureChunk":0}]}